WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.834 --> 00:00:01.835
Deputy Coles: 
You're free to go.

00:00:03.212 --> 00:00:04.713
♪♪

00:00:04.713 --> 00:00:09.927
Justin Timberlake:
I play Eddie Palmer, who comes
back home from twelve years of being in prison...

00:00:09.927 --> 00:00:11.345
♪♪

00:00:11.345 --> 00:00:14.264
Justin:
to find everything a bit
different.

00:00:14.264 --> 00:00:16.808
You just got to get yourself back
out there.

00:00:16.808 --> 00:00:19.686
So many people are just discarded
after they come out of prison.

00:00:19.686 --> 00:00:21.355
You were All-USA player two years
in a row.

00:00:21.355 --> 00:00:22.397
(Whistle blowing)

00:00:22.397 --> 00:00:24.983
Yes, sir.
If I can't get a job sweeping
floors,

00:00:24.983 --> 00:00:26.109
what am I supposed to do?

00:00:26.777 --> 00:00:29.947
While trying to find myself I
stumble upon, Sam.

00:00:29.947 --> 00:00:32.491
There's something seriously
wrong with that kid.

00:00:32.491 --> 00:00:34.493
I think I can spice that up a
little.

00:00:34.493 --> 00:00:37.120
Vivian:
His momma took off again. 

00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:40.207
Sam's mother is battling a
pretty extreme drug addiction.

00:00:40.207 --> 00:00:41.708
You wouldn't know where Shelly
is?

00:00:41.708 --> 00:00:43.210
Your guess is as good as mine.

00:00:43.210 --> 00:00:45.337
You sure you can hang on to
him for a little bit longer? 

00:00:46.713 --> 00:00:47.714
Hey Palmer.

00:00:49.716 --> 00:00:52.719
Cheryl Guerriero:
You have this kid who is just
content in being who he is. 

00:00:52.719 --> 00:00:53.720
Cheers!

00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:55.389
Cheryl Guerriero:
He just does what feels natural.

00:00:55.389 --> 00:00:56.807
Cheryl Guerriero:
He dresses a certain way

00:00:56.807 --> 00:00:59.142
and he is very comfortable in his
own skin.

00:00:59.142 --> 00:01:00.560
-Quite an outfit.
-Thanks!

00:01:01.186 --> 00:01:05.357
Justin:
My character sees that he can
make a difference in this child’s life...

00:01:05.357 --> 00:01:07.442
You think maybe we oughta put
something else in there today?

00:01:07.442 --> 00:01:08.777
Eddie:
Grab that loaf of bread.

00:01:08.777 --> 00:01:10.737
...and finds his way through
that action.

00:01:10.737 --> 00:01:11.905
Sam, you’re doing good, huh?

00:01:13.907 --> 00:01:15.158
Real good.

00:01:15.158 --> 00:01:16.618
Fisher Stevens:
This boy gives Palmer

00:01:16.618 --> 00:01:19.413
self-esteem really and Palmer
gives this boy a father.

00:01:19.413 --> 00:01:20.998
(Crying)

00:01:20.998 --> 00:01:22.249
Who did this to you Sam?

00:01:22.249 --> 00:01:23.375
It’s ok, you can tell us.

00:01:25.836 --> 00:01:26.628
Maggie:
What are you going to do...

00:01:28.380 --> 00:01:29.631
...beat up everyone that picks on
him?

00:01:29.631 --> 00:01:31.008
You ain’t nothing but a
criminal.

00:01:32.009 --> 00:01:33.802
Sheriff Coles:
You just couldn’t stay out of
trouble, could you?

00:01:34.136 --> 00:01:35.512
PALMER!!!

00:01:35.929 --> 00:01:38.348
Alisha Wainwright:
It's about the possibility of
someone who

00:01:38.348 --> 00:01:40.767
through adversity can come out
the other side and be better for
it.

00:01:40.934 --> 00:01:43.645
Palmer:
I know what it feels like to be
left alone.

00:01:43.645 --> 00:01:45.105
I will not abandon that boy.

00:01:45.105 --> 00:01:48.525
This is a story about
redemption, acceptance, and
love.

00:01:49.109 --> 00:01:53.322
Second chances are possible and
you can be whoever you want to
be.

00:01:53.363 --> 00:01:56.491
Palmer:
Truth is, I haven't felt like I
was good at anything

00:01:56.491 --> 00:01:58.994
Palmer:
in a long time, until Sam.

